<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92021" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾶ</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1086
			</span></i>, Ion Trag.<i><span class="en">
				66
			</span></i>. [Codd. vary between <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾶ</span>
			and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾴ</span>; only <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾴ </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάι</span>)
			seems to be admitted by <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				156.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				163.20
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾶ</span> is prob. correct
			Attic and 
				Dor.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥᾱᾰ</span>
			whence 
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥῆα</span> (written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεῖα</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήα</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				12.7
			</span></i>), later 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέα</span> (q.v.); cf. 
				Aeol.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρᾷ</span>.]</div>
